# The assembled common-core geometry

The source assembly derives 11.3.7, the common elementary two-core and its
original SL₃ block, odd degree and Sylow placement, and the product and
orthogonal actions in the core normalizer. It preserves the supplied flag,
original quotient maps and independent natural-action markings. The permitted
earlier-source inputs remain with the linear-geometry assembly owner.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith, refs/quasithin.pdf, printed pp.773--774.
-/
